  <prompt>Fourteen AI routes check only that the caller is signed in, then read or write as the BFF's own identity on records the caller names: a chat session pointed at any matter or document, an agent turn on any document, a playbook run on any record id passed as a parameter, a playbook definition by id or name, another playbook's nodes, another user's prompt templates, any matter's name by party search, and a document re-parented onto any record. Make every one of these routes ask, as the caller, about the exact records it will touch, before it touches them, and refuse with the same answer whether the id does not exist or the caller may not use it.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do NOT rename or move FinanceAuthorizationFilter, and do not create a RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter or any other generalized copy of it: reuse it as it is. The rename is follow-up task 170, after the sweep tasks are integrated. Several sweep tasks reuse this filter in parallel, and a move in one of them would conflict with all the others.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 167 (the every-route guard) runs IN PARALLEL with this task. If RouteAuthorizationGuardTests on your branch has no Pending waiver for your routes (167 not yet landed), do NOT add waivers, ledger entries or Permanent waivers, and do NOT add your files to GovernedFiles. Instead, add a table "Route authorization ledger input" to your task note, with one row per route you changed or deleted: the route key exactly as the guard spells it (VERB /path), the mechanism that now decides (filter, probe or impersonation), the deny test (its fully qualified name, proving a caller without rights is refused), and, for a list whose query runs AS the caller, the words "handler decision: query runs as the caller". The main session records these in 167's ledger at integration. If 167 HAS landed on your branch, follow its ledger contract: delete your Pending waivers and set ResolvedBy and ProofTest in the same diff.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (BINDING): delete a route when it has NO caller in the repo AND it is NOT in any published API description; fix it otherwise. Search the repo for OpenAPI documents and Copilot or agent plugin manifests (for example *openapi*, ai-plugin*, *manifest*.json, declarativeAgent*) before you decide. List every deletion, with its no-caller and not-published evidence, in the note and the PR. Delete the services, filters and options that only the deleted routes used. Keep the file census count in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests right if a whole endpoint file goes.</amendment>
    <amendment>Impersonation: never assign ServiceClient.CallerId or CallerAADObjectId outside Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs (task 160 adds the single SDK entry point there, plus an arch rule). For the Web API, impersonate through DataverseWebApiService's existing impersonateSystemUserId parameter (MSCRMCallerID). It refuses Guid.Empty (task 104).</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 applies to /api/ai/prompts (the prompt library, all routes) and to POST /api/ai/document-intelligence/associate-record: delete each one if it has no caller and is not published; fix it otherwise.</amendment>
