  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: BFF endpoint filters (ADR-008), ProblemDetails (ADR-019), Dataverse RetrievePrincipalAccess over OBO through the existing Spaarke.Core and CallerRecordAccessProbe seams, the chat session model (ChatSessionManager, ChatHostContext) and the playbook node engine. Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task, for each of the 19 route keys listed in the background (14 findings):
(1) every record id the route reads or writes app-only (route value, body field, stored session state, or playbook parameter) is authorized AS THE CALLER, with the right the operation needs, before the first app-only read or write;
(2) an id that does not exist and an id the caller may not use produce the same response (same status, type, title, detail, reasonCode and extension keys; only correlation and trace ids, and the request path in `instance`, may differ), and no detail or extension value contains the requested id;
(3) a seam fault, a missing bearer token or an unresolvable caller denies, with no app-only fallback;
(4) authorized callers get today's behaviour;
(5) the deciding gate is an endpoint filter in the route's own fluent chain whose type the route guard credits (FilterMarker) and inspects (Rule B), except the four filter/endpoint pairs named in the constraints, and a real-host test per route proves the route denies a caller with no rights;
(6) the result is proven live in dev by the main session.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Every anchor below was read on branch work/unified-access-control-r2 at b18a7d321 on 2026-10-03 (identical for these files to task/uac-r2-157-b2-r2). Line numbers drift; Step 0 re-verifies them.

THE 19 ROUTE KEYS (as RouteAuthorizationGuardTests formats keys: METHOD + resolved path). F-numbers are the order of findings in the evidence file.
  F0  POST /api/ai/chat/sessions                                  Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs:83
  F1  PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/context              Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs:141 (registered with MapMethods; see GUARD below)
  F2  POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/messages              Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs:98
  F3  POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/dispatch              Api/Ai/DispatchSessionEndpoint.cs:97 (its own "/api/ai/chat" group, :92)
  F12 POST /api/agent/message                                      Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs:35
  F11 POST /api/agent/run-playbook                                 Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs:62
  F13 GET /api/agent/playbooks/status/{jobId:guid}                 Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs:78
  F9  POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/execute                     Api/Ai/PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs:41
  F7  GET /api/ai/playbooks/by-id/{id}                             Api/Ai/PlaybookEndpoints.cs:70
  F7  GET /api/ai/playbooks/by-name/{name}                         Api/Ai/PlaybookEndpoints.cs:59
  F8  PUT /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/nodes/reorder                Api/Ai/NodeEndpoints.cs:79
  F5  GET /api/ai/prompts/{id}                                     Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:46
  F5  PUT /api/ai/prompts/{id}                                     Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:65
  F5  DELETE /api/ai/prompts/{id}                                  Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:76
  F5  POST /api/ai/prompts/{id}/render                             Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:86
  F6  GET /api/ai/prompts (group "/api/ai/prompts" + "/")          Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:35
  F6  POST /api/ai/prompts (group "/api/ai/prompts" + "/")         Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:55
  F10 POST /api/ai/document-intelligence/match-records             Api/Ai/RecordMatchEndpoints.cs:19
