For the two prompt-library collection routes, use whatever exact key the guard's scanner prints.

CHAT SESSIONS (F0-F3: high, high, high, medium). The /api/ai/chat group has only `.RequireAuthorization()` (`ChatEndpoints.cs:69-71`). The routes add `AddAiAuthorizationFilter()`, which extracts ids ONLY from a `DocumentAnalysisRequest`, an `IEnumerable&lt;DocumentAnalysisRequest&gt;` or a bare `Guid` argument (`Api/Filters/AiAuthorizationFilter.cs:130-153`) and passes straight through when it finds none (`:81-85`). On an exception it answers 500 (`:115-123`), and on deny it returns `result.Reason` as the detail (`:102-106`). The chat DTOs are none of the extracted types: `ChatCreateSessionRequest(string? DocumentId, Guid? PlaybookId, ChatHostContext? HostContext)` (`ChatEndpoints.cs:3573`), `ChatSendMessageRequest(Message, string? DocumentId, ..., ChatActiveItem? ActiveItem)` (`:3635`), `ChatSwitchContextRequest(string? DocumentId, Guid? PlaybookId, ChatHostContext? HostContext, IReadOnlyList&lt;string&gt;? AdditionalDocumentIds)` (`:3756`). So the filter decides nothing on all four routes.
  • `CreateSessionAsync` (`:417-462`) checks tenant and owner oid, then `ChatSessionManager.CreateSessionAsync` (`Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs:154-207`) stores DocumentId and HostContext as given, in Dataverse, Redis and Cosmos. When HostContext.EntityType is the analysis sentinel "sprk_analysisoutput" (`ChatSessionManager.AnalysisHostContextEntityType`, `:657`), `ChatDataverseRepository.CreateSessionAsync` (`Services/Ai/Chat/ChatDataverseRepository.cs:68-74`) also writes the sprk_aichatsummary → sprk_analysis lookup to the caller's EntityId, app-only, and `ReviewMemoEndpoints.cs:260-263` later trusts that EntityId as the analysis to read and persist into.
  • `SwitchContextAsync` (`:1343-1395`) checks tenant, session existence and the 5-document cap, then overwrites DocumentId, HostContext and AdditionalDocumentIds (`:1382-1391`).
  • `SendMessageAsync` (`:477-`) passes `request.DocumentId ?? session.DocumentId`, `session.PlaybookId`, `session.HostContext` and `session.AdditionalDocumentIds` to `SprkChatAgentFactory.CreateAgentAsync` (`:748-754`). Downstream, app-only: `PlaybookChatContextProvider.cs:298` and `:407` call `IDocumentDataverseService.GetDocumentAsync` (the app-only `IDataverseService` singleton, `Infrastructure/DI/GraphModule.cs:95`) and put the document's Summary/Tldr, name and type into the system prompt; `:353` loads the session's playbook by id through `IPlaybookService.GetPlaybookAsync` (app-only, no visibility check); `:1034` reads record memory through `MemoryItemStore.ToRecordPromptFragmentAsync` (`Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryItemStore.cs:276`, no caller check); `:339` sets the RAG parent scope from HostContext. Only the full file text is OBO (`DocumentContextService.cs:689-696`).
  • Dispatch (`DispatchSessionEndpoint.cs:97-99`, handler `:127`, body `[FromBody] DispatchSessionRequest? body`) forwards `session.HostContext` to `SessionDispatchOrchestrator` (`Services/Ai/Chat/SessionDispatchOrchestrator.cs:544-546`), whose ContextBinder reads record memory and, for a matter, the Cosmos pinned context (`Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs:841`, `:870`, `:939`). The memory read is keyed by subject only, with no tenant predicate (evidence F3); a caller-rights check on the host record also closes the cross-tenant variant, because a foreign tenant's record id has no rights in the caller's Dataverse.
  • HostContext types in use: `ChatHostContext.EntityType` is normalized by `EntityTypeNormalizer.Normalize` (`Models/Ai/Chat/EntityTypeNormalizer.cs:57-87`): sprk_matter/sprk_project/sprk_invoice and matter/project/invoice/account/contact become the canonical short forms of `ParentEntityContext.EntityTypes` (`Models/Ai/ParentEntityContext.cs:35-66`: matter, project, servicerequest, invoice, account, contact); every other value, including "sprk_workassignment" and the analysis sentinel, passes through unchanged. The analysis sentinel "sprk_analysisoutput" carries EntityId = an sprk_analysis id and is sent by `src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx:1024-1033` (with a documentId). The Console sends `entityContext.entityType` unmodified (`src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx:3176-3182`). The Copilot agent's OpenAPI declares POST /api/ai/chat/sessions with a hostContext (`src/solutions/CopilotAgent/spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml:15`, schema near `:770`). Server-side session minting with a HostContext (no HTTP create, so no create-time gate): `AnalysisEndpoints.cs:1223` (fork), `ComposeService.cs:1192` (matter host), `ChatSessionManager.cs:713`, `AnalysisChatContextEndpoints.cs:107`.
  • Sessions already stored before this fix may carry an unverified HostContext or DocumentId. A check only at write time leaves them usable, and leaves a caller whose access was revoked still reading. So the stored context is ALSO authorized at use time.

AGENT GATEWAY (F11, F12 high; F13 low). `/api/agent` group: `.RequireAuthorization()` (`Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs:30-32`) plus a per-route `AddAgentAuthorizationFilter()`, which only asserts oid and tid claims (`Api/Agent/AgentAuthorizationFilter.cs:54-82`). The route guard lists it in ClaimOnlyFilters with the reason "it serves no document metadata or bytes" (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:1207-1210`); that premise is false for /message and /run-playbook.
  • `HandleMessageAsync` (`:101-`): `request.DocumentId` (`Guid?`, `Api/Agent/AgentModels.cs:10-34`) goes into `CreateSessionAsync` (`:182-188`, `:195-201`) and `CreateAgentAsync` (`:219-231`) with no check. A resumed session (a ConversationReference whose session the caller owns, `:155-189`) brings its stored HostContext, PlaybookId and documents with it; a reference to someone else's session mints a new one. `request.Context` is not read by the handler.
  • `RunPlaybookAsync` (`:372-445`): body PlaybookId (any GUID, no visibility check; the sibling /execute route carries `AddPlaybookAccessAuthorizationFilter`), DocumentId (required) and Parameters go straight to `IPlaybookOrchestrationService.ExecuteAsync`, which the handler drains to completion inside the request.
  • `GetPlaybookStatusAsync` (`:455-508`): `GetRunStatusAsync(jobId)` (`Services/Ai/PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:371-383`) has no owner check, and the 404 detail echoes the jobId (`:470-475`). `PlaybookOrchestrationService` is registered Scoped (`Infrastructure/DI/AnalysisServicesModule.cs:1302`) and `_activeRuns` is an instance field (`PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:61`), which is why the sweep REFUTED the sibling /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId} routes. The same lifetime makes F13 unexploitable today, and also means a second request can never find a run today; it is still closed with an owner comparison, so a later lifetime change cannot reopen it.
  • `PlaybookRunContext.UserId` (`Services/Ai/PlaybookRunContext.cs:117-120`) is documented as the Dataverse SYSTEMUSERID the run targets and feeds the eq-userid FetchXML substitution (`QueryDataverseNodeExecutor.cs:146`, `:186-206`, `:225-233`). The caller's Entra oid must NOT be stored there.

PLAYBOOK RUN (F9 high, and F11's parameter half). `POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/execute` (`Api/Ai/PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs:41-42`, handler `:139-`) carries only `AddPlaybookAccessAuthorizationFilter` (playbook visibility, with a 404/403 split). The handler writes SSE headers itself (`:158-161`) after a 400 for empty DocumentIds (`:150-155`). Body `ExecutePlaybookRequest` (`:452-468`): `Guid[]? DocumentIds`, `UserContext`, `IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string,string&gt;? Parameters`. Its catch writes `ex.Message` into a RunFailed SSE event (`:194-198`).
  • DocumentIds are never authorized; legacy mode loads document metadata app-only (`AnalysisOrchestrationService.cs:378`) and can leak the name through `AnalysisDocumentLoader.cs:205`.
  • Caller Parameters are rendered into every node's ConfigJson (`PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:1239`, `ApplyConfigJsonTemplates` `:2250-2286`) and override node outputs on key collision. The in-repo `Services/Ai/Insights/Playbooks/matter-health-single.playbook.json` (10 uses) and `predict-matter-cost.playbook.json` (3 uses) use `{{matterId}}`, plus `{{tenantId}}` (3 uses) and content tokens such as `{{matterDescription}}`, `{{matterContext}}`, `{{assessments}}`, `{{currentGrade}}`, `{{observations}}`. The matterId uses reach an app-only FetchXML query (`QueryDataverseNodeExecutor.cs:239`), a LiveFact subject, an index filter and an app-only UpdateRecord PATCH of the matter (`UpdateRecordNodeExecutor.cs:201-260`). A non-GUID value in a FetchXML position is also FetchXML injection.
  • HTTP-entry runs leave `PlaybookRunContext.UserId` unset, so `QueryDataverseNodeExecutor.ResolveUserId` (`:186-206`) falls back to any earlier node output carrying a "userId" property, and the Start node binds the caller's Parameters, so the caller chooses the userId. The app-only scheduler path reads `Parameters["userId"]` deliberately (`PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:140-166`, `ExecuteAppOnlyAsync`); that path has no HTTP caller and is not changed. The Insights orchestrator calls `IPlaybookOrchestrationService` directly, not over HTTP, and is not changed.
  • Do NOT attach the existing `AddAiAuthorizationFilter()` to /execute: its `case Guid` branch (`AiAuthorizationFilter.cs:146-148`) would authorize the route's playbook `id` as if it were a document and deny every caller.

PLAYBOOK DEFINITIONS (F7, F8 medium). `/api/ai/playbooks` group: `.RequireAuthorization()` only (`Api/Ai/PlaybookEndpoints.cs:20-22`). GET /{id:guid} (`:48-49`) carries `AddPlaybookAccessAuthorizationFilter`; by-name (`:59`, handler `:328-376`, app-only `PlaybookService.GetByNameAsync` `Services/Ai/PlaybookService.cs:360-440`; its 404 returns the exception message and its 500 returns `ex.Message` at `:374`) and by-id (`:70`, handler `:399-476`, app-only `IPlaybookLookupService.GetByIdAsync`, wrapped in a 5-minute `IEndpointResponseCache` entry keyed (tid, id) at `:434-440`, over a 1-hour cache inside the service) carry nothing. by-id's 404 puts the id in `detail` and `instance` (`:446-469`).
  • Shipped by-id consumers: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useAiSummary.ts:296` (DOCUMENT_PROFILE_PLAYBOOK_ID, the document AI summary) and `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx:658` (SUMMARIZE_NEW_FILES_PLAYBOOK_ID). by-name has no src consumer (deprecation telemetry at `:337-350`).
  • `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs`): reads RouteValues["id"] as a GUID (`:107-114`), answers an empty 404 for a missing playbook (`:118-122`) and a 403 ProblemDetails for a denied one (`:149-161`), an existence oracle; it has no try/catch. It compares `playbook.OwnerId == userId` (`:125`) where OwnerId is Dataverse `_ownerid_value` (`PlaybookService.cs:235`, `:1060-1061`) and userId is the Entra oid (`CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId`, `:97`); `PlaybookSharingService.GetUserTeamsAsync` filters teammemberships by systemuserid (`Services/Ai/PlaybookSharingService.cs:284`) but receives the oid (`:232`, `:244`). If that holds, OwnerOnly denies everyone and OwnerOrSharedOrPublic reduces to sprk_ispublic (sweep "noteworthy" [ai-b], line 134). This task does not silently change that comparison for the sibling routes; see escalation trigger 1.
  • Reorder: `NodeEndpoints.cs:79-80` (group `/api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/nodes`, `:15-17`) carries `AddPlaybookOwnerAuthorizationFilter`, which checks only the ROUTE playbook. `ReorderNodes` (`:307-340`) never checks that each body nodeId belongs to {id}; the siblings do (`node.PlaybookId != id`, for example `:196-200`). `NodeService.ReorderNodesAsync` (`Services/Ai/NodeService.cs:316-341`) PATCHes `sprk_playbooknodes({nodeId})` app-only one by one with no rollback. `INodeService.GetNodesAsync` exists (`Services/Ai/INodeService.cs:17`).

PROMPT LIBRARY (F5, F6 medium). `/api/ai/prompts` group: `.RequireAuthorization()` plus per-route rate limiting (`Api/Ai/PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs:30-32`). No filter of any kind exists for this surface. Get/Update/Delete/Render discard the oid (`var (tenantId, _)`, `:129`, `:174`, `:199`, `:225`); Get's 404 detail echoes the id (`:133-135`). `ExtractClaims` resolves the oid through `CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId` (`:252-259`). `PromptLibraryService.FindByIdAsync` (`Services/Ai/PromptLibrary/PromptLibraryService.cs:322-359`) matches id + tenantId only; `EnforceWritable` (`:408-415`) blocks only Org/System. `ListAsync` (`:51-83`) queries every caller-supplied teamId; `CreateAsync` (`:118-175`) accepts any `OwnerId` for Ownership=Team (`:137-147`). Personal OwnerId = the creator's oid; Team OwnerId = a team id (Step 1 confirms it is a Dataverse team id). Storage: Cosmos "prompts" container, service identity. No src client calls /api/ai/prompts. Mapped unconditionally (`Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:268`).

RECORD MATCH (F10, F4 high). `/api/ai/document-intelligence` group: `.RequireAuthorization()` only (`Api/Ai/RecordMatchEndpoints.cs:14-16`), mapped only when `DocumentIntelligence:RecordMatchingEnabled` (`EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:322`; default false, true in dev per `docs/guides/AI-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md:991`). No src client calls either route; `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/Phase2RecordMatchingTests.cs` calls both.
  • match-records (`:19`, handler `:45-85`): `RecordMatchService` (`Services/RecordMatching/RecordMatchService.cs`) queries spaarke-records-index with the service credential, interpolates `RecordTypeFilter` unescaped into OData (`:92-95`), fetches `MaxResults * 3` with no cap (`:72`), returns RecordId, RecordType, RecordName, MatchReasons for every hit and an untrimmed `TotalMatches` (`:150`); the 500 returns `ex.Message` (`RecordMatchEndpoints.cs:80-83`). The service is also called by the background `AttachmentClassificationJobHandler` (no HTTP caller). Keywords go raw into a Full Lucene query; once rows are trimmed by the caller's rights that only changes which readable rows come back. The trimmed twin is `POST /api/ai/search/records` (task 077): `RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:111-`) checks tenant, body, caller oid and token and publishes the obligation, and `RecordSearchEndpoints.AuthorizeRowsAsync` (`Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs:246-322`, private today) authorizes each row as the caller (`AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync`, Read) within a 50-check budget (`MaxRecordAuthorizationChecks`, `:211`), and sets the count to the returned rows.
  • associate-record (`:29`, handler `:90-157`): `AssociateRecordRequest` carries DocumentId and RecordId as STRINGS. The handler validates presence, parses RecordId (`:117`), maps RecordType through `Spaarke.Dataverse.DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` (in `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs`), then `IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentAsync(request.DocumentId, ...)` (`:131`) app-only; the 500 returns `ex.Message` (`:152-155`). A document is an intermediate for task 156 (core-ancestor stamp of its children), and its file bytes stay in the SPE container chosen at upload (`Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs`, task 155; outcomes `ResolvedSecure` / `ResolvedFallback` / `Unresolved` / `FailClosed` in `SecureContainerDecision.cs:92-115`).

EXISTING ACCESS MACHINERY TO REUSE (read each before choosing; do not fork):
  • Documents, Read: `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` (`Services/Ai/AiAuthorizationService.cs:48-159`) → `IAccessDataSource.GetUserAccessAsync` per document, OBO token, fails closed per document (`:164-217`); `Success` is false for a partial result (`Services/Ai/IAiAuthorizationService.cs:31-32`). Its denial reasons embed the document id (`:113-115`), so a route's deny body must not pass them through.
  • Any record of a named entity set, any right, cached: `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(userId, entitySetName, recordId, token, ct)` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:255-283`; refuses without a token) → `DataverseAccessDataSource.GetRecordAccessAsync`; cached through `CachedAccessDataSource` (60 s, including None: C12, owned by task 132). Preferred on the chat and agent turn path (latency).
  • A declared list of (entity set, id, operation) checks from route or body, one uniform deny, a 400 rejection before any Dataverse call: `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` and its resolver overload `AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(Func&lt;EndpointFilterInvocationContext, FinanceAuthorizationTargets&gt;, FinanceDenial)` (`Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:61-83`, checks `FinanceAuthorizationCheck` `:125-162`, targets `:168-205`, live-pinned set constants `:222-230` including `DocumentEntitySet = "sprk_documents"`, reason codes `:240-256`). Task 130 built it; its type name is historical, its machinery is generic. It is the reference implementation for associate-record.
  • Any record, uncached: `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync` / `GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync` / `GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:212`, `:274`, `:342`; all `virtual`): OBO, WhoAmI, RetrievePrincipalAccess, None (or null) on every fault. RetrievePrincipalAccess carries a ~1.6 s not-found backoff (`NotFoundRetryDelay`, `:101`) that also lands on genuine denials; do not put `GetCallerRightsAsync` on the per-turn chat path. `GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` has no backoff.
  • Team membership: `IPlaybookSharingService.GetUserTeamsAsync(systemUserId)` (`Services/Ai/PlaybookSharingService.cs:275-301`), which returns an empty set on any failure.
  • Required right per operation: `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs`); existing keys include "read", "write", "entity.associate_document" = AppendTo (`:203-213`), "finance.link_invoice" = Write|Append (`:195-201`).
  • Entity sets (never pluralize): `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.TryResolveAuthorizableEntitySet` (`Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:144-155`, `:192`; matter, project, workassignment, invoice and their sprk_ forms) and `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:115-160`, `:174`; the document-association set, LOCKSTEP with DocumentAssociationMap). Neither holds sprk_analysis. The codebase disagrees on the sprk_analysis set name ("sprk_analysises" at `Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:1914`, "sprk_analyses" at `Services/Communication/RegardingNameFields.cs:59`), so it is read from live metadata.
  • Uniform not-found shape: `SessionOwnershipFilter.EvaluateAsync` (`Api/Filters/SessionOwnershipFilter.cs:110-215`): missing, unowned and owned-by-another are ONE 404 with an errorCode and correlationId and no id in the detail (`:195-212`). `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound` (`:280-`) is the record-flavoured equivalent.
  • NOT a record gate: `IMemoryAccessAuthorizer.CanCallerReadRecordAsync` (`Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryAccessAuthorizer.cs:38-65`) checks entity-type privilege only and is itself a sweep finding (row 42) owned by another task. Do not use it here.
  • Rejected for associate-record, with reasons: `EntityAccessFilter` reads the caller from OfficeAuthFilter's `HttpContext.Items` (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:211`), passes through when no target is found (`:233-243`) and checks one record; `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` reads its target from ROUTE values only (`Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:129`).

GUARD (task 074 / 167). `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs`: GovernedFiles `:126-`, Waivers `:378-` (Pending waivers must name their task and are deleted when the route becomes gated; NoWaiverIsStale `:987-`), Rule B `:1106-1186` (a filter passes when its file contains a DecisionServices name, or when every endpoint file attaching it does: the filter/endpoint PAIR rule), ClaimOnlyFilters `:1194-`, DecisionServices `:1274-1296` (includes "AuthorizationService", "IAccessDataSource", "AccessRights", "CallerRecordAccessProbe"), `ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames` `:1886-1896`, `FilterMarker` `:1898-1902` (credits any `.Add*AuthorizationFilter(` or `.Add*AuthorizationFilter&lt;` call). Three consequences for this task:
  (a) `MapCall` (`:1851`) matches only MapGet/MapPost/MapPut/MapPatch/MapDelete, so `group.MapMethods("/sessions/{sessionId}/context", ["PATCH"], ...)` (`ChatEndpoints.cs:141`) is invisible to every rule. (Two out-of-scope routes also use MapMethods: `:154` rename and `:213` tabs.) `SessionOwnershipGuardTests.SessionScopedRoute` (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SessionOwnershipGuardTests.cs:69-71`) matches `Map\w*`, so MapPatch stays covered there.
  (b) `AddAiAuthorizationFilter`, `AddAgentAuthorizationFilter` and `AddPlaybook*AuthorizationFilter` are already credited by FilterMarker, so Rule A already reports most of these routes as gated. Rule A cannot prove this task's fixes; the real-host denial tests and the seeded removals (acceptance criteria) are the proof.
  (c) None of the 8 files is in GovernedFiles today. Task 167 (not authored on this branch at review time) will govern every route file and add Pending waivers for the 82 findings; this task deletes the waivers for its 19 keys if 167 has landed on its branch, and otherwise the main session reconciles them at integration.

