  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route touched. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, a missing bearer token, an unresolvable Dataverse user, a RetrievePrincipalAccess fault, an exception anywhere in the check, or an entity type outside the closed resolution DENIES with the route's uniform deny. No app-only fallback on any path, and no "skip the check" branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9 (binding)">Scope: every route touched. Reads: the caller's own Dataverse rights decide, through the existing seams named in the background. Writes: a rights pre-check as the caller, then the existing app-only write. Lists: trimmed to what the caller can read. Unknown and denied ids get the same answer, by id kind: a playbook id (by-id, by-name, the execute route id, run-playbook body PlaybookId), a prompt template id and an agent run id answer a uniform 404; a record or document id (from a body, stored session state, a playbook parameter or a result row) answers the route family's uniform 403. Within a route, the status, type, title, detail, reasonCode and extension keys are identical for unknown, denied and seam-fault cases of the same id kind; no detail or extension value contains a requested id (`instance`, when present, is the request path and is excluded from the comparison).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / project">Scope: the 19 route keys. Each route's decision runs as an endpoint filter in that route's own fluent chain, before the handler, and never inside ChatSessionManager, SprkChatAgentFactory, ContextBinder, PlaybookOrchestrationService, PromptLibraryService or RecordMatchService, which other callers use app-only or with no HTTP caller (the scheduler, the Insights orchestrator, Compose, jobs). Four exceptions, each a filter/endpoint pair in which the endpoint refuses when the filter's obligation is absent: (a) match-records trims rows in the endpoint after the filter publishes the obligation, exactly as /api/ai/search/records does; (b) the reorder membership check runs in the handler before INodeService.ReorderNodesAsync, as its sibling node routes do; (c) the prompt-library list intersects team ids in the endpoint after the filter resolves the caller's teams; (d) the agent status owner comparison runs in the handler, which is where the run is loaded, after AgentAuthorizationFilter has established the oid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. No new service and no new logical-name → entity-set map. Extend: AiAuthorizationFilter (chat and agent DTOs, stored session context), PlaybookAuthorizationFilter (by-id/by-name/body PlaybookId key sources, a uniform-404 mode, a run mode for DocumentIds and Parameters), RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter (MatchRecordsApiRequest). Reuse unchanged: FinanceAuthorizationFilter's resolver overload for associate-record (EntityAccessFilter and RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter are rejected for the reasons in the background). Exactly ONE new filter class is allowed: `PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter` in Api/Filters, because the prompt library has no filter today and its rows are Cosmos documents with no RetrievePrincipalAccess answer; it carries the three-question justification in the PR with grep evidence, consults `CallerRecordAccessProbe` (so Rule B credits it) and denies with 404. Any other new type is escalation trigger 8. Any new OperationAccessPolicy key carries the three-question justification in the PR with grep evidence and is registered so OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 / task 130">Scope: entity sets. Never derive a set by pluralizing. Use `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.TryResolveAuthorizableEntitySet`, `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`, or `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet` for sprk_documents. Do NOT declare a new logical-name → entity-set map and do NOT add entries to either existing map (EntityAccessFilter's has a lockstep invariant with DocumentAssociationMap; SemanticSearch's widens POST /api/ai/search). The sprk_analysis set (for the "sprk_analysisoutput" host sentinel) is ONE named constant whose value is read from live `EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_analysis')?$select=EntitySetName`, recorded in the task note, and pinned by a test. A map from a playbook PARAMETER NAME to an entity LOGICAL name (for example matterId → sprk_matter) is allowed; it resolves its set through one of the two existing resolvers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: chat host context (F0, F1, F3, F12). The accepted HostContext types are a CLOSED set: the values `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.TryResolveAuthorizableEntitySet` resolves (matter, project, workassignment, invoice and their sprk_ forms), plus the analysis sentinel "sprk_analysisoutput". A HostContext whose EntityType is outside that set (account, contact and servicerequest included, unless Step 1 and escalation trigger 2 add them by owner decision), or whose EntityId is not a GUID, is a 400 before any rights query. Required right on the host record: Read. A non-empty DocumentId or AdditionalDocumentIds entry that is not a GUID is a 400 before any rights query; an empty string is treated as absent. Do not strip a denied HostContext and create the session anyway: deny.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: stored session context (F2, F3, F12). The routes that run a turn (messages, dispatch, agent message on a resumed session the caller owns) authorize the session's STORED HostContext, DocumentId and AdditionalDocumentIds, plus any per-turn DocumentId, every time, before SSE headers are written and before SprkChatAgentFactory.CreateAgentAsync or SessionDispatchOrchestrator.DispatchAsync is called. One shared evaluation is used by these routes and by create/PATCH (no per-route copy). The evaluation is keyed on the request DTO types (ChatCreateSessionRequest, ChatSwitchContextRequest, ChatSendMessageRequest, DispatchSessionRequest, AgentMessageRequest), never on the mere presence of a sessionId, so the filter's behaviour on every other route that attaches AddAiAuthorizationFilter is unchanged. On dispatch, a null DispatchSessionRequest body is denied by the filter, not passed through. Use the cached path (IAiAuthorizationService for documents, AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync for host records), not CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync, on the turn path. The session may be read once and shared with SessionOwnershipFilter through HttpContext.Items to avoid a second read; SessionOwnershipFilter's own decision is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: playbook parameters (F9, F11). On POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/execute and POST /api/agent/run-playbook, before ExecuteAsync: (1) a caller parameter whose name equals, ignoring case, a server-owned key ("userId", "tenantId", plus any other identity key the Step 1 inventory finds) is a 400; (2) every parameter whose name is in the record-identity map (built from the Step 1 inventory; at minimum matterId → sprk_matter) must be a GUID (else 400) on which the caller holds Read (else 403), and Write as well when the playbook contains an UpdateRecord node whose recordId template references that parameter (determined by reading the playbook's nodes through INodeService.GetNodesAsync); (3) a parameter whose value parses as a GUID and whose name is in neither the record-identity map nor an explicit, reasoned non-record list is a 400. The map and the non-record list are pinned by a test and recorded in the task note. DocumentIds: each one Read via IAiAuthorizationService. The app-only scheduler path (`ExecuteAppOnlyAsync`, `PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:140-166`) and the Insights orchestrator's direct calls are not changed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: playbook visibility (F7, F9, F11). Reuse PlaybookAuthorizationFilter's OwnerOrSharedOrPublic decision unchanged in substance, extended to read the key from where each route has it: by-id → route "id" (the stable id mirrors the primary key, which Step 1(e) verifies); by-name → the playbook resolved from route "name" by the existing service; agent run-playbook → body PlaybookId; execute → route "id" as today. On these four routes a missing playbook, a denied playbook and a fault answer the same 404 (the existing empty-404/403 split stays on the sibling routes outside the 19 keys). The decision runs BEFORE by-id's response cache is read. Do NOT change the owner/team identity comparison for any route in this task; that is escalation trigger 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: agent run owner (F13). The HTTP caller's oid is recorded on the run in a NEW property of PlaybookRunContext (for example StartedByOid), never in `PlaybookRunContext.UserId`, which holds a Dataverse systemuserid for the eq-userid substitution. The property reaches PlaybookRunStatus with `[JsonIgnore]`, so GET /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId} and every other status response do not gain it. ExecuteAppOnlyAsync runs have no owner, and an ownerless run answers the uniform 404 on the agent status route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: prompt library (F5, F6). Personal templates: OwnerId must equal the caller's oid. Team templates: the caller must be a member of the OwnerId team, resolved server-side: caller systemuserid via `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync`, teams via `IPlaybookSharingService.GetUserTeamsAsync(systemUserId)`. Never trust the teamIds query or the body OwnerId for membership. Org/System tiers stay readable and renderable by any tenant caller and stay non-writable (unchanged). An unresolvable caller systemuserid or membership yields an empty team set (Personal still works).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: associate-record (F4). Attach `AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(resolver, FinanceDenial.Forbidden)` whose resolver reads the SAME body the handler binds: DocumentId and RecordId must parse as GUIDs and RecordType must resolve through `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (the same lockstep set as DocumentAssociationMap, which the handler already uses), else `FinanceAuthorizationTargets.Reject` with a 400 before any Dataverse call. Checks: Write and Append on sprk_documents(DocumentId) (a new policy key, or an existing key whose name describes the act; "finance.link_invoice" describes linking an invoice and is not reused), and AppendTo on the target ("entity.associate_document"). Holding position, fail closed: after the rights pass and before the write, resolve both the document and the target with `RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync`; when either decision is `ResolvedSecure` or `FailClosed`, the route refuses with 409 and a reasonCode and writes nothing, because the file bytes stay in the old container (the #1038 leak class). That refusal is lifted only by an owner answer to escalation trigger 6.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: match-records (F10). RecordTypeFilter must be one of "all", "sprk_matter", "sprk_project", "sprk_invoice" (else 400 in the filter, and RecordMatchService also refuses any other value before it reaches the OData filter, after Step 1 confirms AttachmentClassificationJobHandler only passes values in that set); MaxResults below 1 or above 50 (the record-search check budget) is a 400; every returned row is authorized Read as the caller through the shared AuthorizeRowsAsync code; TotalMatches equals the number of rows returned. POST /api/ai/search/records behaviour is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: the handlers of the 19 routes. These exception-message responses are replaced with fixed text: `RecordMatchEndpoints.cs:80-83` and `:152-155`, `PlaybookEndpoints.cs:370-375` and by-name's 404 detail, and the RunFailed SSE event in `PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs:194-198`. Every deny is ProblemDetails with a machine-readable reasonCode (the `sdap.access.deny.*` convention, one code per route family; reuse FinanceAuthorizationFilter's codes where they fit).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. All enforcement is in the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at the IAccessDataSource / AuthorizationService / IAiAuthorizationService / CallerRecordAccessProbe (virtual methods) / ChatSessionManager store / INodeService / IPlaybookService / IPlaybookLookupService / IPlaybookSharingService / IPlaybookOrchestrationService / IPromptLibraryService / IRecordMatchService / RecordContainerResolver seams, hosting the REAL `Map*Endpoints` in-process (the pattern of `tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs`). Every new guard is proven to bite by seeding its removal and watching a named test fail; record each seeded removal and its failing test in the task note. No live Dataverse in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite (`tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests`), NetArchTest (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests`) and BOTH integration suites IN FULL (`tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` and `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests`), not just a build. `ChatEndpointsTests`, `Phase2RecordMatchingTests`, `PlaybookByIdEndpointTests` and `PlaybookByNameDeprecationTests` are known to be affected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF: existing routes, extensions of existing filters, one new filter class, no new service) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master from a short path, both sides with Compress-Archive, equal file counts; report both sizes and the delta; ceiling 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred: scope found during execution that is the same defect on the same surface is added to this task. Live Dataverse is READ-ONLY during development (metadata and inventory reads are allowed); every live write and the live gate are run by the main session. Use existing non-admin test users in their current BU; if a gate needs a user at a specific access level, ask the owner to create one (round 4 item 1).</constraint>
  </constraints>

