    <patterns>
      <pattern name="per-route declared checks, uniform deny, 400 before Dataverse" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:61-205">Each route declares where its ids come from and which right each needs; there is no fallback chain; a declaration with no check denies.</pattern>
      <pattern name="uniform not-found with errorCode, no id echo" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/SessionOwnershipFilter.cs:110-215">Missing, unowned and owned-by-another are one 404; the log is the only place the cases differ.</pattern>
      <pattern name="filter publishes the obligation, endpoint trims rows" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:111-; src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs:246-322">Caller identity and token checked in the filter; each row authorized Read as the caller in the endpoint; count equals rows returned.</pattern>
      <pattern name="in-process contract host over the real endpoint mapper" location="tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs">Minimal WebApplication, fake auth scheme, real Map*Endpoints, substituted access seam.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Run /conflict-check (ChatEndpoints.cs, SprkChatAgentFactory.cs, AgentEndpoints.cs, the filters named in the constraints). Re-verify every anchor in the background. Confirm or refute, by reading code, that PlaybookAuthorizationFilter compares an Entra oid with a Dataverse systemuserid (escalation trigger 1). Check whether task 167 has landed on the branch.</step>
    <step order="1">Inventory (read-only; record everything in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-164-ai-route-authorization.md): (a) every HostContext EntityType value and every DocumentId / AdditionalDocumentIds value source that a shipped client or server path sets (grep src/client, src/solutions, src/server for hostContext, entityContext and new ChatHostContext), and which table each DocumentId names; (b) every consumer of session.HostContext, session.DocumentId, session.AdditionalDocumentIds and session.PlaybookId that reads app-only (refine, restore, suggest, review-memo, summarize and others), whether the session PlaybookId's definition reaches the prompt (PlaybookChatContextProvider.cs:353), and whether any tool reads the ActiveItem record or a dispatch Args record id app-only; (c) every `{{...}}` token in node ConfigJson that a caller parameter can fill, from `Services/Ai/Insights/Playbooks/*.json` and from live sprk_playbooknode rows (read-only), with the node type and whether it is a record identity, a write target, an identity key, or free text inside a FetchXML / filter / recordId position; (d) the live entity set name for sprk_analysis; (e) whether the Document Profile and Summarize New File(s) playbooks (useAiSummary.ts DOCUMENT_PROFILE_PLAYBOOK_ID, DocumentEmailWizard.tsx SUMMARIZE_NEW_FILES_PLAYBOOK_ID) are sprk_ispublic, and whether every live sprk_analysisplaybook row's sprk_playbookid equals its primary key; (f) that Team prompt OwnerIds are Dataverse team ids; (g) the callers of /api/agent/*, /api/ai/chat/sessions and /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/execute in the Copilot agent OpenAPI and their parameters; (h) the RecordTypeFilter and MaxResults values AttachmentClassificationJobHandler passes to RecordMatchService.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend AiAuthorizationFilter with the shared chat-context evaluation (body DTOs for create, PATCH, messages, agent message; stored session context for messages, dispatch and a resumed agent session), the closed host-type resolution, the GUID validation, and one constant deny body per route family. Change the PATCH /context registration from MapMethods to MapPatch. Attach the filter to POST /api/agent/message. If Step 1(b) shows the session PlaybookId's definition reaches the prompt, also attach the extended PlaybookAuthorizationFilter (body PlaybookId) to create and PATCH /context, subject to escalation trigger 1.</step>
    <step order="3">Extend PlaybookAuthorizationFilter: key sources for by-id, by-name and body PlaybookId, and a uniform-404 mode used on by-id, by-name, execute and agent run-playbook; a run mode for execute and agent run-playbook (DocumentIds Read, the parameter rules). Attach it to by-id, by-name and agent run-playbook. Record the HTTP caller's oid on the run (new property) and compare it in GET /api/agent/playbooks/status/{jobId}, with a 404 that does not echo the jobId.</step>
    <step order="4">Reorder: in the handler, load the playbook's nodes through INodeService.GetNodesAsync and refuse before any PATCH when a body nodeId is foreign, unknown or duplicated.</step>
    <step order="5">Prompt library: add PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter (ownership and team membership per the constraint) to the {id} routes and create, and use it as a filter/endpoint pair for list.</step>
    <step order="6">Record match: extend RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter for MatchRecordsApiRequest; share AuthorizeRowsAsync; validate RecordTypeFilter and MaxResults; fix the count. associate-record: attach FinanceAuthorizationFilter's resolver overload per the constraint; add the secure-boundary holding refusal; wire task 156's cascade or record the path for it.</step>
    <step order="7">Correct the ClaimOnlyFilters reason for AgentAuthorizationFilter in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests to a true statement (an identity precondition; the per-record decisions on /message and /run-playbook are made by AiAuthorizationFilter and PlaybookAuthorizationFilter in the same chain). If task 167 has landed on the branch, delete the Pending waivers for the 19 keys and make sure Rule A, Rule B, NoWaiverIsStale and the census pass; otherwise record the 19 keys in the note and the PR for the main session.</step>
    <step order="8">Tests per the acceptance criteria, including the seeded removals; update the ChatEndpointsTests, Phase2RecordMatchingTests, PlaybookByIdEndpointTests and PlaybookByNameDeprecationTests fixtures.</step>
    <step order="9">Build; affected, full BFF unit, NetArchTest and both integration suites in full; publish size and CVE per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
    <step order="10">Write the manual live gate procedure into the task note for the main session (ids redacted to the first 8 characters). Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` only after the code criteria pass; the live gate stays marked pending until the main session runs it.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>PLAYBOOK IDENTITY DEFECT. Step 0 confirms PlaybookAuthorizationFilter compares the Entra oid with Dataverse _ownerid_value (and passes the oid to GetUserTeamsAsync), AND Step 1(e) shows the Document Profile or Summarize New File(s) playbook (or any playbook a shipped client, including the Copilot agent, fetches by id or runs) is not sprk_ispublic. Attaching the decision to by-id would then break the document AI summary or the document email wizard for everyone. STOP and present per CLAUDE.md §6: (a) RECOMMENDED: fix the comparison inside PlaybookAuthorizationFilter by resolving the caller's systemuserid (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync`) and passing it to the owner comparison and the sharing check; this also restores intended owner and team access on about ten sibling playbook routes, which is a behaviour change outside this task's findings; (b) mark the system playbooks shipped clients fetch as public (a data change, a main-session live write). Do not skip the check on by-id.</trigger>
    <trigger>STABLE-ID MIRROR. Step 1(e) finds a live playbook whose sprk_playbookid differs from its primary key. The by-id decision keyed on the route id would then deny a playbook the lookup can find. STOP and list the rows; do not key the decision on an unverified assumption.</trigger>
    <trigger>HOST-TYPE OR ID VOCABULARY. Step 1(a) shows a shipped client or server path sets a HostContext EntityType the closed resolution cannot map (for example account, contact, servicerequest, sprk_event, sprk_communication), sends a non-GUID DocumentId, or sends a DocumentId that names a table other than sprk_document. STOP and list each with its source; denying it would break a shipped surface, and widening an existing map needs an owner decision (CLAUDE.md §11 lockstep).</trigger>
    <trigger>PARAMETER VOCABULARY. Step 1(c) or (g) finds a record-identity token whose entity type cannot be determined from its name, a GUID-valued parameter a shipped caller (including the Copilot agent) sends that the rules would refuse, a write node other than UpdateRecord that targets a caller parameter, or a non-identity caller parameter that fills a FetchXML, filter or recordId position. STOP and propose the map entries, refusals or rights; do not guess.</trigger>
    <trigger>AGENT TOKEN. The live gate shows the Copilot agent's inbound token cannot be exchanged OBO, so every agent turn with a document is denied. STOP and report; do not add an app-only fallback.</trigger>
    <trigger>PROMPT TEAM IDS. Step 1(f) shows Team OwnerIds are not Dataverse team ids (for example Entra group ids), so membership cannot be decided with GetUserTeamsAsync. STOP and present options: (a) retire the Team tier routes (no src client calls /api/ai/prompts); (b) resolve membership another existing way. Do not trust the caller's teamIds.</trigger>
    <trigger>SECURE RE-PARENT. The owner wants associate-record to move documents across a secure boundary, or a shipped caller of associate-record appears. STOP and present the container question: the file bytes stay in the old SPE container, so a move needs task 155/156's container resolution before the 409 holding refusal can be lifted.</trigger>
    <trigger>STRUCTURE. The fix appears to need a new service, a second new filter class, a new logical-name → entity-set map, an edit to FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs, or an ADR exception (for example ADR-008 or ADR-013 on placing a check inside Services/Ai). STOP and raise it per CLAUDE.md §6.5 with the three paths.</trigger>
    <trigger>CONSUMER BREAK IN THE LIVE GATE. A legitimate reader is denied: the analysis wizard's session create (Read on the sprk_analysis it just created), a Compose session turn (Read on the document's matter), the Console on a record the user can open, the document AI summary, or the document email wizard. STOP and report the right that failed; do not widen to app-only or drop the check.</trigger>
    <trigger>SCOPE GROWTH. Step 1(b) finds more than the in-scope routes consuming the stored session context app-only. Add each to this task when the same shared evaluation closes it (owner no-deferral rule); STOP only if one needs a different rule or a client change.</trigger>
    <trigger>MERGE CONTENTION. /conflict-check shows an open PR from chatendpoints-decomposition-r1 or spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4 that moves or restructures the chat routes or SprkChatAgentFactory, or another sweep surface task has an unmerged edit to AiAuthorizationFilter or PlaybookAuthorizationFilter. STOP and agree the merge order before editing those files.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Document Read: `IAiAuthorizationService` (`Services/Ai/AiAuthorizationService.cs`), already behind `AiAuthorizationFilter`. Record rights: `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:255-283`) and `CallerRecordAccessProbe` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs`). Filters already attached to or built for these surfaces: `AiAuthorizationFilter` (decides nothing for chat DTOs), `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter` (route id only), `RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter` + `RecordSearchEndpoints.AuthorizeRowsAsync` (task 077, the trimmed twin of match-records), `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (task 130, declared multi-record body checks with a uniform deny). Entity sets: `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.TryResolveAuthorizableEntitySet`, `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`, `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet`. Team membership: `IPlaybookSharingService.GetUserTeamsAsync`. Uniform deny: `SessionOwnershipFilter.EvaluateAsync`, `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound`. Container decision: `RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync`. Prompt library: grep of `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/` and `PromptLibraryEndpoints.cs` finds no filter of any kind on /api/ai/prompts.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for every surface except the prompt library. Chat, agent and playbook gates extend filters already attached to those routes; match-records extends the record-search filter; associate-record reuses FinanceAuthorizationFilter's resolver overload unchanged. The prompt library cannot extend an existing filter: every owner-comparison filter is bound to its own store (SessionOwnershipFilter to chat sessions, JobOwnershipFilter to Office jobs), and the record filters ask Dataverse about Dataverse rows, while a prompt template is a Cosmos document. So one new filter, `PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter`, compares the stored owner with the caller's oid and resolves team membership through existing seams. Other new surface: possibly one OperationAccessPolicy key for Write|Append on a re-parented document, one named sprk_analysis set constant, one parameter-name → logical-name map for playbook record parameters, and one non-serialized owner property on the run context. Each carries the three-question justification in the PR.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any signed-in user can: have the Assistant repeat the record memory, pinned context and stored AI summary of any matter or document, secure records included (F0-F3, F12); run any playbook against any matter id with app-only queries and an app-only write onto the matter, and choose the userId its queries run under (F9, F11); read any private playbook definition (F7); rewrite execution order on other users' and system playbooks (F8); read, overwrite, delete or plant other users' and teams' prompt templates (F5, F6); find secure matters' names and ids by party name (F10); and re-parent any document onto any record, moving it out of or into a secure matter (F4). Without the prompt-library filter, F5 and F6 have no place to attach a per-route decision that the route guard can see.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

