  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">F0 POST /api/ai/chat/sessions: a body HostContext the caller cannot Read, and a body DocumentId the caller cannot Read, each return the chat family's uniform 403; the response is identical (per the goal's comparison) for a non-existent id, an existing unreadable id and a seam fault, and contains neither id; ChatSessionManager.CreateSessionAsync is not invoked (no Redis, Cosmos or sprk_aichatsummary write). A caller with Read on both gets 201 as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F0 validation: a HostContext EntityType outside the closed set, a non-GUID HostContext EntityId, or a non-empty non-GUID DocumentId returns 400 and no rights query is made. The analysis sentinel "sprk_analysisoutput" is authorized as Read on the live-verified sprk_analysis entity set, and a test pins that set name and asserts it reaches the seam.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F1 PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/context: DocumentId, each AdditionalDocumentIds entry and HostContext are each authorized Read; if any one is denied the route returns the uniform 403 and the session is unchanged (UpdateSessionCacheAsync not invoked). The route is registered with MapPatch, still carries AddSessionOwnershipFilter, and SessionOwnershipGuardTests passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Chat session PlaybookId (F0, F1): if Step 1(b) shows the session playbook's definition reaches the prompt app-only, a body PlaybookId the caller may not access is denied with the chat family's uniform 403 and nothing is stored; otherwise the note records the evidence that it does not, and no code changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F2 POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/messages: the effective document (request.DocumentId, else session.DocumentId), session.AdditionalDocumentIds and session.HostContext are authorized Read before any SSE header is written; on denial the route returns the uniform 403 as ProblemDetails (not an SSE stream) and SprkChatAgentFactory.CreateAgentAsync is not invoked. A session whose HostContext was written straight into the session store (a pre-fix session) is denied the same way. A reader gets the SSE stream as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F2 ActiveItem: if the Step 1 inventory shows a tool on the messages path reads the ActiveItem record app-only, an ActiveItem the caller cannot Read is dropped from the turn (test); otherwise the note records the evidence that nothing reads it and no code changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F3 POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/dispatch: the session's stored HostContext, DocumentId and AdditionalDocumentIds are authorized Read before SessionDispatchOrchestrator.DispatchAsync; on denial the route returns the uniform 403 as ProblemDetails before any stream, and neither the orchestrator nor the ContextBinder memory/pin reads run. A null body is denied by the filter. Dispatch Args record ids are handled per the Step 1 inventory (authorized, or the note records that none is read app-only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Revocation (F2, F3, F12): a session created while the caller held Read on its host record is denied on its next messages, dispatch and agent-message turn after the seam reports None for that record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F12 POST /api/agent/message: a body DocumentId the caller cannot Read returns the uniform 403 before any session is created or resumed and before CreateAgentAsync; a resumed session (ConversationReference owned by the caller) whose stored HostContext or document is unreadable returns the uniform 403. A reader gets 200 as today. The route's fluent chain carries AddAiAuthorizationFilter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AiAuthorizationFilter on other routes: on every route outside the 19 keys that attaches AddAiAuthorizationFilter, the filter's behaviour is unchanged (the existing AiAuthorizationFilterTests pass unmodified, and a test shows a refine or history request with no new DTO type takes the existing path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F11 POST /api/agent/run-playbook: a body PlaybookId that does not exist, one the caller may not access, and a playbook-lookup fault return the identical 404 (no id in the body); an unreadable DocumentId returns the uniform 403; the parameter rules below apply; on every denial IPlaybookOrchestrationService.ExecuteAsync is not invoked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F13 GET /api/agent/playbooks/status/{jobId:guid}: tested through a substituted IPlaybookOrchestrationService (the Scoped lifetime means a real second request never finds a run): a run whose recorded owner is a different oid, an ownerless run and an unknown jobId return the same 404; no body contains the jobId; the caller whose oid is recorded gets 200. A PlaybookOrchestrationService test shows ExecuteAsync records the HTTP caller's oid in the new property and leaves `PlaybookRunContext.UserId` unset, and a serialization test shows PlaybookRunStatus JSON does not contain the owner.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F9 POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/execute: every DocumentIds entry is authorized Read; any unreadable entry returns the uniform 403 before SSE headers and before ExecuteAsync; a missing, denied or faulting playbook lookup returns the identical 404; the route's {id} is never authorized as a document (test: a readable document plus a playbook id in the route passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Parameters (F9 and F11): a parameter named userId or tenantId in any letter case returns 400; a record-identity parameter that is not a GUID returns 400; one the caller cannot Read returns 403; one targeted by the playbook's UpdateRecord node that the caller cannot Write returns 403; a GUID-valued parameter in neither the map nor the non-record list returns 400; in every case ExecuteAsync is not invoked. A caller with the required rights runs as today. A test pins the map and the non-record list, and the note lists the inventory they came from.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F7 GET /api/ai/playbooks/by-id/{id}: the playbook access decision runs before the response cache is read; a denied playbook, a non-existent id and a decision fault return the identical 404 with no id in the detail; an allowed caller gets 200. A test shows an allowed caller warming the cache does not let a denied caller read the cached entry. PlaybookByIdEndpointTests pass with their hosts updated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F7 GET /api/ai/playbooks/by-name/{name}: the same decision applies to the playbook the name resolves to; a denied playbook and an unknown name return the identical 404 with no name or exception message in the body; the 500 path returns no exception message. PlaybookByNameDeprecationTests pass with their host updated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F8 PUT /api/ai/playbooks/{id:guid}/nodes/reorder: a body containing any nodeId that belongs to another playbook or does not exist returns one uniform answer (404) and INodeService.ReorderNodesAsync is not invoked (zero PATCHes); duplicate nodeIds return 400; a body whose nodes all belong to {id} returns 204 as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F5 GET, PUT, DELETE /api/ai/prompts/{id} and POST /api/ai/prompts/{id}/render: another user's Personal template, a Team template of a team the caller is not a member of, and a non-existent id return the same 404 (same status, title, detail without the id, reasonCode); no ReplaceItemAsync or DeleteItemAsync is issued. The owner, or a team member, gets today's behaviour. Org/System templates stay readable and renderable, and PUT/DELETE on them still return 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F6 GET /api/ai/prompts?teamIds=: only teams the caller is a member of are queried (no Cosmos query is issued for a non-member teamId); when the caller's systemuserid or membership cannot be resolved, Team templates are empty and Personal templates are still returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F6 POST /api/ai/prompts with Ownership=Team: an OwnerId naming a team the caller is not a member of (or when membership cannot be resolved) returns 403 and no item is created; a member creates as today. Personal create is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F10 POST /api/ai/document-intelligence/match-records: only rows the caller can Read are returned, authorized through the same AuthorizeRowsAsync code as /api/ai/search/records; TotalMatches equals the number of rows returned; a RecordTypeFilter outside the closed set returns 400 and the OData filter never sees it (RecordMatchService test); MaxResults below 1 or above 50 returns 400; a request with no bearer token returns 401; a row whose check faults is dropped; the 500 path returns no exception message. /api/ai/search/records tests (including RecordSearchRowAuthorizationContractTests) stay green unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F4 POST /api/ai/document-intelligence/associate-record: a caller lacking Write or Append on the document returns 403; a caller lacking AppendTo on the target returns 403; unknown and denied ids answer identically; a non-GUID DocumentId or RecordId, or a RecordType outside EntityAccessFilter's set, returns 400 before any rights query; a secure or fail-closed container decision on either side returns 409 with a reasonCode; on every one of these, UpdateDocumentAsync is not invoked. A caller with all rights and no secure side gets 200 as today. The 500 path returns no exception message. FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs is unchanged in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fail closed, every family (chat, agent, playbook, prompt library, record match): with no bearer token forwarded, and with the access seam throwing, each route returns its family's uniform deny and makes no app-only read or write (asserted on the substituted seams). Unauthenticated requests still return 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Real-host denial: for each of the 19 route keys, a test through the REAL Map*Endpoints host shows that a caller the substituted seam reports as None (or, for the prompt library and agent status, a caller who is not the owner) is denied on that route. A test that invokes a filter class directly, or only asserts a mock was called, does not satisfy this criterion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeded removals: for each new decision (chat-context body, chat-context stored session, playbook key sources, playbook uniform 404, playbook run DocumentIds, playbook parameters, agent status owner, reorder membership, prompt ownership, prompt team membership, match-records row trim, match-records filter validation, associate-record document right, associate-record target right, associate-record secure refusal), removing it locally makes a named test fail; each removal and its failing test are recorded in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Route guard: the ClaimOnlyFilters reason for AgentAuthorizationFilter in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests no longer claims the agent routes serve no document data; every filter type that makes a decision on the 19 keys (including PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter) is credited by FilterMarker and passes Rule B. If task 167 has landed on the branch, no Pending waiver remains for any of the 19 keys and Rule A, Rule B, NoWaiverIsStale and the census pass; if not, the PR and the note say so and list the 19 keys.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reuse: the only new type is PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter; no new service and no new logical-name → entity-set map exist; EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType and SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets are unchanged (the diff adds no entries); IMemoryAccessAuthorizer is not used by any of the 19 routes' decisions; the sprk_analysis set name used in code equals the live value recorded in the note; OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests passes, including any key this task adds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the tests cover exactly the behaviours above plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints (missing oid, missing token, seam fault); anything beyond that has a one-line justification in the task note. No test uses Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, checks DI registration or checks constructor null arguments.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Suites: BFF build green; the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest and BOTH integration suites (tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests) pass in full, with ChatEndpointsTests, Phase2RecordMatchingTests, PlaybookByIdEndpointTests and PlaybookByNameDeprecationTests updated where the new rules change their inputs. Publish size reported against a fresh origin/master build per CLAUDE.md §10 (both sizes, delta, zip tool, equal file counts) and at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev; run by the main session; existing non-admin test users in their current BU; results in the task note with ids redacted to 8 characters): (a) a user with no Read on matter M and document D: POST /api/ai/chat/sessions with hostContext M, and with documentId D, return 403, and the same body as for a random GUID; (b) a reader of M creates a session hosted on M and gets an Assistant reply; (c) PATCH /context to M by the non-reader returns 403 and the session still points at its old context; (d) POST /messages with documentId D by the non-reader returns 403 before any stream; (e) the analysis wizard creates its session for the analysis its user just created, with no warning; (f) a Compose document session gets a reply; (g) the document AI summary (useAiSummary by-id) and the document email wizard's summarize step (DocumentEmailWizard by-id) still load for a normal user; (h) if RecordMatchingEnabled is true in dev: match-records by the party name of a matter the user cannot read returns no row for it, and associate-record of D onto M by a user without Write on D returns 403 and D's lookups are unchanged on read-back; (i) user B cannot GET, PUT, DELETE or render user A's Personal prompt template (404); (j) if the Copilot agent is deployed in dev, an agent turn on D by the non-reader is denied; if not, record "not available" and do not substitute.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner round 9 (2026-10-03): the route authorization sweep is fixed in full by UAC-r2, critical and high first, one access-control pattern everywhere; overlaps with other projects are coordinated through /conflict-check and GitHub issues, not handed off. This task's 14 findings are sweep rows 18 (agent message, F12), 19 (agent run-playbook, F11), 23 (PATCH context, F1), 24 (session create, F0), 25 (messages, F2), 29 (playbook execute, F9), 31 (match-records, F10), 32 (associate-record, F4), 53 (dispatch, F3), 54 (node reorder, F8), 55 (by-id / by-name, F7), 56 (prompt list / team create, F6), 57 (prompt {id} routes, F5), 78 (agent status, F13).
Facts found at authoring and review that the sweep did not state: (1) the guard's MapCall regex does not see MapMethods, so PATCH /context (and the out-of-scope rename and tabs PATCH routes) is invisible to Rule A; (2) AddAiAuthorizationFilter, AddAgentAuthorizationFilter and AddPlaybook*AuthorizationFilter are already credited by FilterMarker, so Rule A cannot prove these fixes and task 167's Pending waivers for these keys would read as stale on day one unless 167 changes how those filters are credited; (3) F13 is unexploitable today because PlaybookOrchestrationService is Scoped (the same reason the sibling runs routes were refuted); it is still closed; (4) F8 is probably unreachable today because the OwnerOnly filter compares an oid with a systemuserid (escalation trigger 1); the membership check is still added so a fix to the filter cannot reopen it; (5) a forged "sprk_analysisoutput" HostContext also binds the caller's session to another user's sprk_analysis (ChatDataverseRepository.cs:68-74), which ReviewMemoEndpoints then trusts; the F0/F1 write-time check closes that path for new sessions and the turn-time check covers stored ones only on the turn routes, which is why Step 1(b) inventories review-memo and summarize; (6) a second shipped by-id consumer exists (DocumentEmailWizard.tsx:658); (7) PlaybookRunContext.UserId is a systemuserid feeding eq-userid, so the run owner needs its own property; (8) the codebase holds two different sprk_analysis set names, so the live value decides.
Related work owned elsewhere: the insights routes (sweep rows 17 and 40) share the playbook Parameters mechanism; whichever task lands second reuses the first's parameter rules. The memory routes (rows 42, 43, 68) own IMemoryAccessAuthorizer and the pins. The analysis routes (rows 1, 2, 22, 50-52) own AnalysisAuthorizationFilter and sprk_analysis access.
Review amendments 2026-10-03 (adversarial review against the code): see the main session's review record for the list of changes (associate-record moved from EntityAccessFilter/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter to FinanceAuthorizationFilter's resolver overload; one new PromptLibraryAuthorizationFilter allowed because no filter exists for the prompt library; uniform 404 extended to /execute; run owner kept out of PlaybookRunContext.UserId and out of serialized status; DocumentEmailWizard added as a by-id consumer; stable-id mirror trigger added; FetchXML-position parameters added to the parameter trigger; anchors corrected).</notes>

